--
N5008 [range.adaptor.object], [over.match.oper]/3: `arr | views::take(3)'
selects the constrained operator|(_Range &&, _Self &&) of libstdc++ 16's
range adaptors.  The front end rejects that candidate and falls back to
the built-in `|', converting `arr' to `_Partial' through its variadic
converting constructor ("conversion from 'signed int [5]' to 'struct
_Partial': implicit arithmetic conversion not permitted").  With
libstdc++ 13 (cpp20_ranges_basic) the same program verifies.  cvise
reduction (/tmp/r163/red/kb_L16rng, kb_L16rng2) of cpp20_ranges_basic
preprocessed with GCC 16.2.1's headers; not reduced further yet (540
lines; the reduced loop no longer computes the sum, so the test only asks
that the unit converts).  The file uses GCC 16's built-in type traits (__decay,
__remove_cvref, ...): g++ 16 accepts it (with -O1 it links and runs, printing only
the WRONG failure; the reduction left std::forward undefined); g++ 13 and clang++ 18 reject
it for those built-ins.  Pre-existing (fails on bin53).
